@nsobid-592C7051A4E620563D0296096D8F0AC5

# Splatoon 2 5.5.2 - Disable anti-aliasing

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables every post-process anti-aliasing pass.
//
// All of the game's AA is agl::pfx::FilterAA, drawn at the end of
// gsys::ModelSceneBuffer::drawFinalImage. Its modes are FXAA, ReduceAA and a
// draw callback. The game's GfxMgr binds its own SMAA (edge detection, blend
// weights, neighborhood blending) to that callback when it loads a scene, so
// SMAA, not FXAA, is the AA normally drawn.
//
// Whether the filter runs is one test: the scene allows AA, the filter is
// enabled, and its scale is above zero. It is inlined into each function that
// plans or draws the frame: calcView picks the scene's render target,
// allocRenderBuffer sizes it, and drawFinalImage routes the image through the
// filter. Each copy now takes its false result, so the scene renders straight
// to the final target as it does when a scene turns the filter off, and no AA
// pass runs whatever mode or parameters a scene or environment file selects.

@enabled
01803738 05000014   // B to the AA-off result in calcView (was LDR S0,[X,#0xE48] = FilterAA scale)
01805078 08000014   // B to the AA-off result in allocRenderBuffer (was LDR S0,[X,#0xE48] = FilterAA scale)
0180539C 05000014   // B to the AA-off result in drawFinalImage (was LDR S0,[X,#0xE48] = FilterAA scale)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Splatoon 2 5.5.2 (agl/gsys + Lp + sead,
// NVN). The retail build is symbol-stripped; every site was matched to the
// symbol-bearing 1.1.0 QA build by structure and byte-verified against the IDB
// before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
